# Goal — report the outcome of the move just executed, then get the next directive.
# (On the first call nothing has executed yet: success defaults true, observation empty.)
bool success        # did the move just executed (plan + follow) succeed? (ignored on the first call)
string observation  # grounded VLM feedback from the execution, verbatim (the planner's path reasoning)
string mission_path # optional: load this mission YAML before advancing; empty keeps the current one
bool first          # true on the FIRST advance of a fresh tree run -> wipe any prior narrative and reseed. The MissionAdvance BT leaf latches this per run (fresh leaf instance per ExecuteTree goal); an explicit signal, NOT inferred from an empty observation (a mid-run move can legitimately report nothing)
---
# Result — the next directive
bool mission_done    # true when the mission is over (complete OR failed)
bool mission_failed  # true when it ended in failure (stuck in an environment past the cycle cap); false on clean completion
string description   # the next instruction to feed path_planner (empty when mission_done)
string area          # the current environment (from the narrative)
string message       # the narrative's present intent, closing summary, or the failure reason
# The unified image buffer for this cycle, owned here (oldest first, last = current
# view). The BT forwards it to PlanPath.images so the planner plans over the
# SAME frames the director just judged — one buffer, no mismatch. Empty when mission_done.
sensor_msgs/CompressedImage[] images
---
# Feedback
string state         # "RUNNING" while judging / (re)planning
